[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:88. Trapped in a Mine]
[00:00.600]Passage 88 | 文章八十八
[00:02.310]Trapped in a mine. | 困在矿井里。
[00:04.960]Six men have been trapped in a mine for 17 hours. | 六名男子被困在矿井里已有17小时。
[00:10.255]If they are not brought to the surface soon, | 如果他们不尽快被带到地面，
[00:13.185]they may lose their lives. | 他们可能会丧命。
[00:15.560]However, rescue operations are proving difficult. | 然而，救援行动进展困难。
[00:20.345]If explosives are used, | 如果使用炸药，
[00:23.200]vibrations will cause the roof of the mine to collapse. | 震动将导致矿井顶部坍塌。
[00:27.480]Rescue workers are therefore drilling a hole on the north side of the mine. | 因此，救援人员正在矿井北侧钻孔。
[00:33.480]They intend to bring the men up in a special capsule. | 他们打算用一个特殊的舱室将这些男子运上来。
[00:38.125]If there had not been a hard layer of rock beneath the soil, | 如果土壤下面没有坚硬的岩层，
[00:42.680]they would have completed the job in a few hours. | 他们几个小时内就能完成这项工作。
[00:46.035]As it is, | 事实是，
[00:47.400]they have been drilling for 16 hours, | 他们已经钻探了16个小时，
[00:50.485]and they still have a long way to go. | 而且他们还有很长的路要走。
[00:53.715]Meanwhile, a microphone, which was lowered into the mine two hours ago, | 同时，两个小时前放入矿井的一个麦克风，
[00:59.050]has enabled the men to keep in touch with their closest relatives. | 使得这些人能够与他们最亲近的亲属保持联系。
[01:03.470]Though they are running out of food and drink, | 尽管他们的食物和饮料快用完了，
[01:06.895]the men are cheerful and confident that they will get out soon. | 但这些男子心情愉快，并相信他们很快就能出去。
[01:11.760]They have been told that rescue operations are progressing smoothly. | 他们被告知救援行动进展顺利。
[01:16.590]If they knew how difficult it was to drill through the hard rock, | 如果他们知道钻穿坚硬的岩石有多困难，
[01:21.495]they would lose heart. | 他们就会失去信心。